# [[.Title]]

A [Nectar UI](https://[[.Engine]]) app.

```sh
CGO_ENABLED=0 go run .     # run
nectar dev                 # run, restart on code changes (state kept), live assets
go test ./...              # tests (headless, no window needed)
CGO_ENABLED=0 go build     # build ./[[.Name]]
```

Update the engine with `go get [[.Engine]]@latest && go mod tidy`.

## Build the desktop app

```sh
nectar build                              # this OS (macOS: universal .app)
nectar build -os windows -arch amd64      # cross-build a Windows .exe
nectar build -os linux -arch arm64
```

Results go to `dist/`:

| OS | You get |
|---|---|
| macOS | `dist/[[.Title]].app`: Info.plist, `.icns` icon, universal binary (arm64 + amd64), ad-hoc signed |
| Windows | `dist/[[.Exe]].exe`: icon, DPI-aware manifest, and no console window (`-console` keeps it) |
| Linux | `dist/[[.Exe]]-linux-<arch>/`: binary, `.png` icon, `.desktop` entry, `install.sh` |

- **App name, id, version and icon:** set in `nectar.json`.
- **Changing the icon:** replace `assets/icon.png` with your own square PNG (1024×1024 is best). `nectar icon -seed "#0B57D0"` regenerates the default one.
- **Distributing on macOS:** sign with your Developer ID and notarize. The ad-hoc signature only works on your own Mac.

## Structure

```
main.go                      opens the window, runs app.New()
nectar.json                  app name, id, version, icon (for nectar build)
assets/                      embedded resources (main.go mounts them: WithResources)
├── assets.go                go:embed list (add new top-level folders here)
├── icon.png                 app icon, 1024×1024
└── images/welcome.png       read with widgets.AssetImage{Name: "images/welcome.png"}
internal/
├── app/                     root widget, navigation shell, routes
│   ├── app.go               theme + state wiring
│   ├── shell.go             app bar + navigation rail
│   └── routes.go            top-level pages (add yours here)
├── theme/                   the look: seed color, light/dark themes, type tweaks
│   ├── theme.go
│   └── tokens.go            spacing and radius tokens
├── state/                   app-wide state (Settings) shared via Provider
├── components/              reusable widgets (Page layout, Section card)
└── pages/
    ├── home/
    └── settings/
tests/                       headless UI tests (tap, type, find text)
```

- **Change the brand color:** `theme.Seed` in `internal/theme/theme.go`. All M3 color roles are generated from it, for both light and dark.
- **Add a page:**
  1. Create `internal/pages/<name>/<name>.go` with a `Page` widget.
  2. Add a `Route` for it in `internal/app/routes.go`.
- **Share state:** add fields to `state.Settings` (keep the struct comparable). Read them with `state.Of(ctx)` and change them with `state.Update(ctx, func(s *state.Settings){…})`.

Widgets come in three shapes, and a widget is whichever interface it implements:

- `Build(ctx) Widget` for stateless composition
- `CreateState()` for stateful widgets. Call `s.SetState(func(){…})` to rebuild.
- `CreateRenderObject` / `UpdateRenderObject` for custom layout and paint
